      "id": "claim",
      "title": "The idea",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "The picture of Africa as a continent of villages is old and sticks. Village life is real for very many people. It is not the whole picture.",
              "editorial": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "reveal",
          "prompt": "Think first: out of every 100 Africans, how many do you think live in towns and cities?",
          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "About 45, in 2023, counted by adding the countries' own urban figures.",
              "cite": [
                "wb-urban-2023",
                "wb-population-2023"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "count",
      "title": "What the numbers say",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "stat",
          "items": [
            {
              "value": "45%",
              "label": "of about 1,478 million people lived in urban areas",
              "cite": [
                "wb-urban-2023",
                "wb-population-2023"
              ]
            },
            {
              "value": "23 of 54",
              "label": "countries where most people were urban",
              "cite": [
                "wb-urban-2023",
                "wb-population-2023"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "In 2023 about 672 million people in the 54 countries lived in urban areas, out of about 1,478 million.",
              "cite": [
                "wb-urban-2023",
                "wb-population-2023"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": " That is about 45%, calculated here by adding the countries' figures.",
              "cite": [
                "wb-urban-2023",
                "wb-population-2023"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "In 23 of the 54 countries, more than half the people were urban.",
              "cite": [
                "wb-urban-2023",
                "wb-population-2023"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": " Counted this way, the other 31 were mostly rural.",
              "cite": [
                "wb-urban-2023",
                "wb-population-2023"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "range",
      "title": "Two very different Africas",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "The urban share runs from about 17% in Malawi to about 92% in Gabon.",
              "cite": [
                "wb-urban-2023",
                "wb-population-2023"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": " Niger, South Sudan and Ethiopia are below 25%; Libya is at 88%.",
              "cite": [
                "wb-urban-2023",
                "wb-population-2023"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "So \"most Africans live in villages\" is true of some countries and false of others, and the share moves with every year.",
              "editorial": true
            }
          ]
